After playing for years, I finally ascended. Can't believe it. Need to
share.

It was so straightforward. Found an elven dagger early on, turned it
into a +5 Sting so I'd be ready when I got Magicbane. Didn't get
Magicbane by sacrificing--had to wish for it, using the wand in the
Castle--and used it as my primary weapon thereafter. Found spellbooks
of finger of death, cancellation, and create familiar early on, but
only ended being able to cast finger of death reliably (and learned
that if a creature had reflection, it wasn't that useful. Tried to use
a pet Archon instead of my ring of conflict in but he or she was eaten
by a purple worm. (Other pets: an orange dragon--a dog that ate a
chameleon--was also eaten and digested, and a golden naga--a cat who
stepped on a polymorph trap by accident--got killed at the front door
of the castle while I went around the back.

Instead of the blessed Archon figurine, should've wished for a can of
grease, because I fell into Rodney's moat and ruined a collection of
scrolls (mostly remove curse) and spellbooks (reason to stash them
instead of carrying them in a BoH). Didn't have much trouble with
stuff getting cursed on my way back up from the bottom, except my
towel, which I used one of my three potions of holy water to fix; that
let me bless my unicorn horn once I met Pestilence--the other one
boiled and exploded when I was hit with a wand of fire. Ended up going
to all three altars before finding the chaotic one, where I sacrificed
the amulet. Unfortunately, hit the high priest of Anhur with a wand of
fire while trying to take out the white dragon blocking the door, so I
had no friends inside the temple at all.

Thank Anhur for the ring of conflict--I wouldn't have gotten through
the crowds of bad guys (especially on the Plane of Earth and the
Astral Plane--at a certain point everybody seems to have scrolls and
wands of create monster). Feels like cheating to set them against each
other like that, but whatever.

Also, I don't know when I got crowned. Didn't happen through
sacrificing--found a potion of enlightenment around level 47 and
discovered that it had happened w/o my knowledge. All I got from
praying was luck and the "play the right tune" advice, which I didn't
bother with; why would you when you can blow the door and use a scroll
of earth to fill in the moat? I thought that was strange, to get
crowned like that.

Only once had a character get the Amulet, a healer who had left his
levitation boots in a cursed bag of holding below the Castle. When he
got to the Plane of Air, he spun around uselessly while monsters
crowded around him. Won't make that mistake again. He sacrificed again
and again, piling up artifact weapons until finally getting Magicbane,
but in the process kept forgetting his spells and eventually wore his
spellbooks out. Won't make that mistake again, either.


Anyway, here's the dumplog, if you're interested. I'd bronze it if I
could. Btw, somebody on the Astral Plane had Frostbrand, found
Demonbane in a bones pile, and my Archon left Sunsword behind when he
was eaten. I never used any of them--no skill slots. Same with a
silver sabre, which turned out to be less useful than Magicbane
against demons because I didn't know how to use it and was expert in
dagger. I left it behind to keep from getting burdened.

shabadoo99, chaotic male elven Wizard


